  "music": "w1-doodle-docks",
  "authorNotes": "Two players, three checkpoints, four segments — every prop and gap type World 1 has, in one long run. Seg 1: a plain swing, same shape as 01/02, gets both players moving. Seg 2 is 06's combine again: carry crate-w1-08-a onto rope-w1-08 for a heavier, more forgiving swing across the second gap; relic-w1-08-a was picked up back at spawn and is still being carried through this whole segment, which is the point — the gauntlet is as much about not dropping cargo as it is about the gaps. Seg 3 is the hardest: board patrol lift-w1-08 (timed, 300px back-and-forth), ride it to its far side, then repeat 07's throw — swing-anchor-08 anchors one player while the other is thrown the remaining ~410px to pier C, where relic-w1-08-b waits. Seg 4 is a plain swing home, both relics and both players arriving together. All four gaps carry assist beams (the seg-3 one drawn thicker, same convention as 07) for a party that wants to trade the Clock objective for a guaranteed finish this deep into the level."
